# Code Simplicity

- When writing or editing code, make it as simple as possible while keeping code quality high.
- Prefer direct, readable implementations over clever abstractions.
- Add abstractions only when they clearly reduce real duplication or complexity.
- Keep public APIs small and obvious.
- Avoid over-engineering, speculative extensibility, and unnecessary indirection.
- Write code based on software development best practices.
- Preserve tests and type clarity for behavior that matters.
- Prefer function and method names that start with a verb describing the action they perform.
